    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** leading the charge as our premier option at a 77.36 rating. Despite the uncertainty of his pending lineup spot, his capacity to exploit the 4.82 xERA of Rhett Lowder makes him our most bankable asset. He is closely shadowed by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.34), who benefits significantly from a +10% park factor and a favorable platoon advantage against Basso. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) rounds out our top-tier tier; his massive 19% SP skill adjustment against Sugano makes him a high-efficiency start, as he continues to be a cornerstone for our production in the middle of the order.\n\nWhile we are navigating a stretch of injuries to key contributors like **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**, we have managed to maintain competitive output by leveraging platoon advantages. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) is a particularly strong play today; beyond his base projection, the combination of a 16% park boost and wind blowing out at his venue gives him the highest ceiling among our corner infielders. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (58.04) remains a marginal start; while his SP skill adjustment against Kent is favorable, the -13% platoon drag against the left-handed starter necessitates caution regarding his efficiency for our daily cap.\n\nThe tightest decision on the roster involves the outfield and utility spots, where **Sam Antonacci** (55.50) and **Drake Baldwin** (53.32) narrowly edged out fringe considerations. **Nasim Nunez** (52.46) remains in the lineup primarily for his defensive utility and potential to contribute to our scarcity-driven SB goals, despite a score that dipped due to his lower-order placement. We are monitoring the status of **Gunnar Henderson** closely, as his absence from the lineup continues to leave a void in our core production, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining healthy active roster. We will keep a watchful eye on any late-inning weather alerts, but as it stands, the lineup is set to maximize our 5x5 Roto efficiency.",
